  "opportunity_definition": "At actual action, positive capped cost and latest bet/raise setter is the named opponent. Calls do not replace setter; a companion raise does. Blind-only limp prices excluded. Counts are decisions plus unique hands; repeated raises can create several decisions in one hand. Direct observation means Hero has not folded at that event; spectator means Hero folded. Joint flop requires both survived preflop and a flop was actually dealt, regardless of later folds.",
  "limitations": [
    "AI textual strategy experience only, not human/UI",
    "single reviewer and fixed continuous 100-hand sample per opponent",
    "different deals and model actions, not controlled paired strategy comparison",
    "all players reset to 100BB each hand; no adaptation to bankroll accumulation",
    "unshown opponent holes remain unknown",
    "some Hero read-label mistakes and debatable loose bluff-catches are disclosed in interactive-review.md"
  ]
